# Copyright (C) 2026 Daniel Jameson. GPL v3 or later.
#
# The same syntax as cpmtools' diskdefs file (bundled alongside as "cpmtools-diskdefs"), so any definition here
# can be copied into a cpmtools diskdefs file and vice versa. Extra keys, which cpmtools ignores:
#   heads N        physical sides (default: 2 if tracks > 86 and even, else 1; "sides" also implies 2)
#   secbase N      first sector ID, used when making a new disc (default 1)
#   imdmode N      ImageDisk mode for a new disc: 0/1/2 = FM 500/300/250 kbps, 3/4/5 = MFM 500/300/250 kbps
#   desc "text"    description shown in menus
#   source "text"  where the definition comes from and how far it has been checked
# and a top-level line
#   describe NAME "text"   gives a description to a definition loaded later (e.g. from cpmtools' file).
# A definition here replaces a cpmtools definition of the same name.

diskdef acorn-z80
  desc "Acorn Z80 second processor, CP/M 2.2, 400K (80 track double-sided, FM)"
  source "Acorn Application Note 007: 3 reserved tracks, 128 entries, side 1 runs back from track 79, 512-byte logical sectors from pairs 0/1 4/5 8/9 2/3 6/7. Block size inferred from the 388K stated. Checked on three real discs (Colossal Cave, CP/M installation discs 1 and 2), which also have the DFS catalogue Acorn's CP/M puts on track 0."
  seclen 256
  tracks 160
  heads 2
  sides outback
  sectrk 10
  skewtab 0,1,4,5,8,9,2,3,6,7
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 128
  boottrk 3
  acorndfs yes
  secbase 0
  imdmode 2
  os 2.2
end

